; TERM.term.un — the paths term-entry shape (re-cut 2026-08-08 per steward
; verdict: the survey-driven template "failed rather miserably" against a
; ~20-line 2022 sketch, lexicon-middleman's episode.yml — which is the spine
; here. Diagnosis kept for the record: the survey optimized field coverage;
; the target was reading experience. 90% payload, 10% apparatus.)
;
; ACCEPTANCE TEST (the five-second glance): a steward reading a term they have
; never seen knows (1) what to call it, (2) what not to call it, (3) what it
; is, (4) what must be true of it — before any apparatus appears.
;
; SHAPE — above the fold, in order:
;   :word        the term itself                                    {1,1}
;   :alternates  spelling/morphological variants of the same word   {0,1} list
;   :synonyms    other words legitimately used for this concept     {0,1} list
;   :avoid       flat negative prescription — never these words     {0,1} list
;                (a rename's old designation goes HERE, e.g.
;                 universal-path :avoid [universal-location])
;   |quote       evocative external grounding — ONLY where one      {0,1}
;                genuinely earns its place; never padded
;   <body>       the definition: ONE sentence, plain prose, sibling
;                terms referenced inline as [[term/x]] links        {1,1}
;   |invariants  plain-English bullets that ARE the relations —     {0,1}
;                prose that carries structure (below)
;
; Below the fold (apparatus, each defended by one sentence of demand):
;   :status      settled | carved | open | weak | deprecated  — steward comb state
;   :defined-by  segment slug — D5's projection needs the authority pointer
;   :anchor      span name in that segment — D5's grain
;   |note :audience maintainer / |open — workflow + open questions, never rendered
;
; INVARIANT PHRASINGS (controlled, few — the diagram tools parse exactly
; these; anything else is free prose, kept but not graphed):
;   "Is a kind of [[term/X]]"                          → containment (Euler)
;   "Every <word> is exactly one of [[A]] or [[B]]"    → partition (Euler)
;   "Mutually exclusive: [[A]] | [[B]] | …"            → pairwise disjoint
;   "Is the dual of [[term/X]]"                        → dual pair-binding
;   "Belongs to [[term/X]]"                            → part-of, one
;   "Has exactly one|at most one|one or more|zero or more [[term/X]]"
;                                                      → has {1,1}|{0,1}|{1,N}|{0,N}
;   "<Verb phrase> exactly one|… [[term/X]]"           → typed edge, same arities
;   "… exactly one of: a | b | c" (after a target)     → closed manner enum
;   leading "(pending <slugged cite>) "                → suspended relation:
;                visible, cited, non-structural until the steward rules
;
; The one thing prose-carrying-structure must not blur (the specimen that
; forced this re-cut): "Is a kind of X" is NEVER "made of X" — an act HAS
; one or more descriptors; a description IS one kind of descriptor.
